  <name>Echo Weather</name>
  <summary>Atmospheric meteorological desktop application</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Echo Weather is an atmospheric desktop application built with GTK 4 and Cairo,
      bringing weather forecasts to Linux desktops.
    </p>
    <p>Key Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Real-time weather data and 16-day forecasts powered by Open-Meteo</li>
      <li>Adaptive weather canvas with dynamic precipitation, clouds, and celestial effects</li>
      <li>Detailed atmospheric metrics including UV index, humidity, visibility, pressure, and air quality</li>
      <li>Integrated lunar calendar with phases and moonrise times</li>
      <li>Multi-location management with disk caching for instant responsiveness</li>
      <li>Support for both light and dark desktop themes</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.dezaetterg.EchoWeather.desktop</launchable>
